<!-- waiho — `<<~ waiho name value>>body<<~/waiho>>` binds `name` for the body's duration (block-scoped).
     `<<~! waiho name value>>` (lar-pragma-pattern, PRAGMA_HAND_KEPT loop 2) carries no closer: it
     hoists to the top of the carrier's execution context, immutable by convention
     (api/pono/waiho.mem #/law) — a genuinely DIFFERENT posture from the block form, not a cosmetic
     `!` variant, so it rides its own pattern field/eventType rather than folding into open/close. -->

\procedure ~waiho(p1:"" p2:"" p3:"")
<$set name=<<p1>> value=<<p2>>><$transclude $variable="~" name=<<p3>>/></$set>
\end
